              "id": "CVE-2026-55798",
              "name": "LanguageSpecificPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "python-pillow: Pillow: Arbitrary command injection via shell metacharacters in file paths"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Pillow is a Python imaging library. Prior to 12.3.0, WindowsViewer.get_command() constructed a cmd.exe shell command by directly embedding a file path into an f-string without escaping and passed the result to subprocess.Popen(..., shell=True), allowing shell metacharacters in the file path to inject arbitrary cmd.exe commands. This issue is fixed in version 12.3.0."
